From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: run gpu_prerast triangle fans in the GPU chunk loop,
 opt-in, on v10+ biblioklept

Two kinds of fans over the gpu_prerast arena were not handled: indexed
fans with primitive restart (dropped as gpu_prerast_unhandled: the CPU
split cannot see where a restart starts a new hub) and indirect fans
(lowered in one pass, clamped to the arena since the previous patch).
Indirect fans over 2048 instances also ran as one grid.

With PANVK_FAN_CHUNKS=1 (Android: debug.mesa.panvk.fan.chunks=1) both
run in gpu_prerast_chunk_loop() like strips. Off (the default),
nothing changes.

- panlib_fan_chunk_step (fan_chunks.cl) plans each chunk: whole
  instances when one fits max_verts (at most 2048), else a window of
  one instance. A window that cuts a fan keeps its hub: the next
  window is [hub, i .. i + max_verts - 2] with i the last vertex of the
  one before, so every API triangle is drawn once with its vertices,
  winding and primitive ID (the CPU fan split does the same).
- With restart the window is scanned with the whole workgroup (as
  chunk_scan does for strips). A window that holds a restart and does
  not reach the end ends at its last restart; the fans in it are drawn
  whole from their own hubs and the next window starts after it. The
  window of a cut fan is scanned from i - 1, a vertex of that fan, so
  its first fan counts the hub. The primitive counts are exact, so
  prims_done gives the GS primitive ID base and primitives generated.
  Each window moves on by at least one position: the loop ends.
- panlib_fan_chunk_fill writes the chunk as 32-bit indices into a
  per-draw buffer of max_verts + 1 entries (element numbers for
  non-indexed fans, whose vertexOffset is then firstVertex; restart
  indices as 0xffffffff). The chunk is always drawn as an indexed fan
  of that buffer: c->draw is the 5-word indexed layout, firstIndex 0.
- Direct fans without restart keep the CPU split.
- Restart fans in polygon line/point mode stay off the chunk loop: the
  polygon kernel walks back to the hub per vertex, quadratic in a
  max_verts chunk (the pattern of the 120 GS hang).

The fan state is its own struct (fan_chunks.h) next to struct
panlib_chunk_draw, and the kernels are in fan_chunks.cl, so tess_draw.h
and draw_helper.cl, which jm-v9 patches later in the series, keep their
lines. The switch is a DEBUG_GET_ONCE option in the csf draw file, not
a PANVK_DEBUG flag, for the same reason.

Build-only; not device-tested.

